Patch 0014-draft-head-per-batch.patch for vLLM, base commit 8e2beaa3bff595577a069d49d96bde9074294ec2 (vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-8e2beaa3bff595577a069d49d96bde9074294ec2).
What: Adds draft_token_map_max_rows to the speculative config: the sparse draft head (vllm#59740's token map) drafts only for steps with at most that many rows (one per running request), and the 65,536-row NVFP4 draft head drafts above it. The sparse head's dynamic rows cost time per row: they pay with one request and not with six. Unset, the token map is used at every batch size.
Upstream: no vLLM PR. written for this recipe.
This file modifies vLLM (Apache-2.0); the vLLM copyright and SPDX lines in the files it changes are kept.

